OL,3,AUncontrolled AI could lead to 'silicon
OL,4,Aspecies' rivalling humans, warns
OL,5,AMicrosoft
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe head of Microsoft AI has warned
OL,8,Fthat without adequate safeguards, the
OL,9,Fdevelopment of AI could lead to the
OL,10,Femergence of a new "silicon species"
OL,11,Fwhich competes with humans.
OL,13,FMustafa Suleyman said rival firm
OL,14,FAnthropic is treating AI like it is
OL,15,Fhuman, an approach he called
OL,16,F"misguided" which could create
OL,17,Ftechnology that humanity cannot
OL,18,Fcontrol.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1789669133
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AUncontrolled AI could lead to 'silicon
OL,4,Aspecies' rivalling humans, warns
OL,5,AMicrosoft
OL,6,
OL,7,FSpeaking to the BBC's Today programme,
OL,8,Fthe chief executive said it was "right"
OL,9,Ffor people to be concerned about AI,
OL,10,Fbut there were "very practical things
OL,11,Fthat we can do" to control it.
OL,13,FThe comments are the latest in a series
OL,14,Fof stark warnings from the AI industry
OL,15,Fabout the technology's possible
OL,16,Fdangers. Anthropic has been approached
OL,17,Ffor comment.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
